RENDERING TIPS TO ADD:
dirty rectangles
only loop through the area that needs to be changed lol
the CPU cycles for computing that area are WAY less then those used looping the whole screen
only update that element if it needs to be changed
have a LIST of rects that gets cleared every frame and gets added to only by elements that could change that area.

Multi-level font atlas:
have multiple font sheets and change depending on resolution ( might add later b/c don't wanna deal with a million font sizes rn)

Double buffering:
allocate a 2nd area of memory in ram the same size as the screen, once that frame is drawn, copy it to lfb_ptr

bit-shift alpha blending:
unsigned int blended_color = ((fg_color * alpha) + (bg_color * (255 - alpha))) >> 8; (do 3x for the 3colors)

use virtual to physical scaling to scale without streatching on any asp rto
virtual_to_physical_scale = (float)height / 1000.0f;
note: right edge will keep changing so be dynamic about boarders
note: does NOT keep aspect ratio. to deal with aspect ratio utilize calculable offsets (ex screen center or 1/4 from right 1/2 from top) for static objects and for dynamic objects, utilize a static offset as a starting point then store dynamic variables such as the abstracted x and y values
omg this HURTS idk how people do graphics design for a living ;w;

use painters algerithm to have only 1 buffer


